    "full_chapter_only_diff": "--- original/chapter09\n+++ source12/chapter09\n@@ -716,5 +716,5 @@\n     ids = order + [\"none\"]\n     p = scores.softmax(-1)\n-    chosen = min(range(len(ids)), key=lambda i: (-float(p[i]), ids[i]))\n+    chosen = min(range(len(ids)), key=lambda i: (-float(scores[i]), ids[i]))\n     return dict(zip(ids, p.tolist())), ids[chosen]\n \n",
    "direct_original_claim_ids": [
      "g2-error-cost-conventions"
    ],
    "original_claim_statement": "17.2 的捨入誤差與9.16人工成本是不同量；它們不自動等於訓練loss。",
    "current_cost_source_quote": "用人工訂的成本說明：開錯頁的成本是5單位，開對是0；先澄清固定花1單位，並暫時假設問一次就能解決這一輪的不確定。若 p 是經過校準、可以用來估算答對機會的機率，直接開頁的**期望成本**是 `5*(1-p)`：開錯的成本5乘上開錯的機率 1−p，再加上開對的成本0乘上 p；澄清則固定是1。在 p 大於0.8時，前者較小；剛好相等時由事先訂的規則處理。這個門檻只屬於這張簡化的成本表；換成轉帳這類做錯成本大得多的動作，成本表不同，門檻也必須重算。",
    "current_glossary_cost_quote": "| 誤差、成本 | 17.2 把原值與還原值的差叫捨入誤差；9.16 做決策時，人工替每種結果與做法訂的單位數叫成本（例如開錯頁 5 單位）。兩者和代價（loss）是不同的量 | [17.2](chapters/17.md#17.2)、[9.16](chapters/09.md#9.16) |",
    "cost_claim_reason": "The registered r-ch09 support is the artificial cost5 convention in9.16. Both9.15 and9.16 remain byte-identical, so the statement that this manual decision cost differs from training loss still holds.9.17 changes only how an artificial candidate winner is selected, not a cost unit, loss definition, cost table or empirical measurement.",
    "linked_pointer_original_claim_ids": [
      "g4-pointer",
      "g4-pointer-permutation"
    ],
    "current_glossary_pointer_quote": "| pointer head（指向式計分頭） | 用問題表示與候選表示的投影比較，替在場選項打分；重排性質取決於表示、位置與readout，不能只看點積公式 | [9.17](chapters/09.md#9.17)、[20.14](chapters/20.md#20.14) |",
    "pointer_support_reason": "Personally inspected the old/new9.17 complete linked mechanism and current pointer glossary row. Shared projections, candidate visibility, symmetric none, causal contrast and permutation qualification are unchanged. Selecting raw scores then stable ID preserves the explicitly intended highest-score/stable-tie rule directly; finite-precision softmax probabilities need not preserve distinct-score resolution. It adds no learned quality or general permutation guarantee. Original pointer claims and their pinned Kev/Transformer support remain valid.",
